# Workflow Guardrails

## Trigger
Apply on every coding/planning session before implementation and before session close.

## Hard constraints
- Never implement directly on `develop`.
- Never skip `advance-after-pr-close` after PR merge.
- Never finalize session memory from invalid state.
- Never run `git init` in this cloned repository.

## Required checks
Run before coding:
- `git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree`
- `git remote -v`
- `git branch -a`
- `git status -sb`

Run workflow checks:
- `./scripts/load-work-report.ps1`
- `./scripts/validate-pre-implementation.ps1`

## Blocking behavior
- If current branch is not `develop` at bootstrap time, normalize with:
`./scripts/load-work-report.ps1 -AutoNormalizeBaseBranch`
- If tree is dirty and no explicit exception is approved, block implementation.
- If close session is blocked, do not write memory until guardrails pass.

## Exception controls
- Diagnostics: `-DryRun`
- Dirty tree exceptions: `-AllowDirty`, `-AllowDirtyNormalize`, `-AllowDirtyClose`
- Every exception must be explicitly stated back to the user.
